stered in `datasette/default_actions.py`, right after `create-table` and `drop-table`.\n- **Mapping:** `decision_for_write_sql_operation` in `datasette/write_sql.py` maps the two statements to those actions.\n- **Spurious delete:** in `datasette/utils/sql_analysis.py`, dropping a view no longer adds a `delete-row` requirement. I renamed `dropped_tables` to `dropped_tables_and_views`.\n- **Docs:** `docs/authentication.rst` lists both actions in the `--root` permissions and has a section for each.", "ttft_ms": 4076, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 36449, "uuid": "ab6ee821-b46e-4e64-be32-40987bd18e15", "ttft_stream_ms": 3580, "time_to_request_ms": 52, "first_content_frame_ms": 3580, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
